sts/boost_drift_replay.py`'s recorded 3379.1 s is more than half the table: one indivisible script over half the total makes the predicate unsatisfiable for EVERY lane plan. The fix adds the sound second arm (a plan whose wall equals the heaviest single script is provably optimal) and, because the diff touches the GATE_FILE `tests/closure.py`, this PR's `closures` job runs the FULL arm, re-records every script on CI Linux, and `closures-autofix` merges the fresh CI-recorded table onto this branch — the sanctioned re-record path; no recorded second is hand-edited.\n\n## Head\n\n4d6d329e57d1f1557b4571b36d3134cbbcf4e48d\n\n## Mutation proof\n\nTwo mutations, both reverted; selftest green at the head after each revert.\n\n1. The pin restored to its old form (`2*max < sum`, no second arm) on the current main table — the defect reproduces:\n   `python3 tests/closure.py selftest`\n   `FAIL MUTATION the planned max lane is under half the table's recorded seconds  [max 3379.1s, total 6059.1s]` / `1 of 101 closure shrink pins FAILED`\n2. `lane_plan` forced to `lanes = 1` (degenerate single-lane plan) with the amended pin — the pin refuses it; the second arm is not an always-true escape:\n   `python3 tests/closure.py selftest`\n   `FAIL the planned max lane is under half the table's recorded seconds, or equals the heaviest indivisible script no plan can beat  [max 6059.1s, total 6059.1s, pole 3379.1s]` / `2 of 101 closure shrink pins FAILED` (the generic LPT-balance pin fails alongside it).\n\n## Null control\n\nThe unmodified tree at origin/main d5f584152: `python3 tests/closure.py selftest` → `1 of 101 closure shrink pins FAILED`, exactly the pin above. Evidence dir `/private/tmp/fix-closure-pole-ev/` carries both runs' output.\n\n## Figures\n\n- `python3 tests/closure.py selftest` at the head → `ALL 101 closure shrink pins PASSED`.\n- `git show 282054566 -- tests/closures.json` → the pole's provenance: the only two recorded-seconds entries the bot changed on PR #2142 were `boost_drift_replay.py` 1489.6→3379.1 and `features.py` 288.5→598.2.\n- `python3` diff of the `recorded` tables at 282054566 vs a618171a1 → the six entries that differ move 2.07–2.56x together (boost 2.27x, features 2.07x, backtest 2.31x, validate 2.56x, edge 2.14x, block_duty 2.33x); every other entry is byte-identical.\n- `python3 tests/structure.py` at the head → `STRUCTURE RATCHET PASSED` (16 metrics at or under budget; structure.py's own metrics are untouched — the one budget leaf this branch raises is ci_budgets.json's coord_footprint, named under Red checks and Approval).\n\n## Red checks\n\n`fast (3.14)` — red on every PR re-derived against main since #2142 merged. Root cause and countermeasure are this PR: the cheaper detector is the pin itself, which caught the unsatisfiable table within the 3 s selftest; the main-data cause is a recorded table whose pole exceeds half its total, and the countermeasure is the pin's optimality arm (data alone can never make the invariant unsatisfiable again) plus the FULL-arm re-record this gate-file diff forces, which lands CI-recorded seconds for every entry including the pole. The same context is also red on a second, independent main-data defect this head's history records: the entities null control (archscore.coord_footprint 2592 derived vs the committed 2587 row #2118 grew without re-recording) — answered by the re-record commit carried in this branch (4d6d329e5, ci_budgets.json 2587->2592, recorded_at pinned to the derivation head 4787610ad; verified red-first on main, 2279/2279 green on the branch carrying it). The two fixes were deadlocked — each PR's merge commit lacked the other's fix — so the re-record rides here and #2175 lands after as the record of the deliberate raise, reviewed separately at its own head.\n\n`budget-raise-gate` red until tvofi approves at the head carrying 4d6d329e5 (a cap went up: `tests/ci_budgets.json` `archscore.coord_footprint` 2587 -> 2592): the cheaper detector is the ratchet itself, which already fired on main and is the reason this re-record exists; the standing cost is zero new checks — the gate's own rule (0013) is the control, and the owner's approving review at the pushed head is the answer it requires.\n\n## Approval\n\nThe cherry-picked commit 4d6d329e5 is a raise in a `*_budgets.json` (tests/ci_budgets.json: archscore.coord_footprint 2587 -> 2592, recorded_at pinned to the derivation head 4787610ad): per budget-raise-gate (0013) it merges only on the owner's approving review at the head this branch carries. The orchestrator posts that review under mandate 6151222764, covering both the pin change and this raise explicitly at the pushed head. This seat does not merge and does not approve.\n\n## Sequencing note\n\nCommit 4d6d329e5 is the re-record branch's commit cherry-picked verbatim (same tree change as #2175 at 2da1d3a6b) to break the circular required-context dependency between this PR and #2175; the owner review at this head covers both changes explicitly.\n\n## Forward-carry\n\nThe SLOW_GATED design choice for the owner: with a pole legitimately near half the table, the full arm's wall is the pole's lane and lane balance is exhausted; excluding `tests/boost_drift_replay.py` from the planned set (SLOW_GATED membership like `tests/rolling.py`) would change what the gate runs and needs owner review. Recorded on #201 (comment 6151632320); not done in this PR.\n\n## Friction\n\nnone\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T18:10:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T20:45:22Z","closed_at":"2026-10-13T20:45:20Z","merged_at":"2026-10-13T20:45:20Z","merge_commit_sha":"664a4c05e3ead3100e252d3f2f2a0b4cdd230e00","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2173/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_optimizer/pulls/2173/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tvofi/heatpump_o